iv></div></a></figure></div><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7Sbv!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb8e4f62c-a946-4705-9128-65a5d82af519_4032x3024.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7Sbv!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb8e4f62c-a946-4705-9128-65a5d82af519_4032x3024.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7Sbv!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb8e4f62c-a946-4705-9128-65a5d82af519_4032x3024.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7Sbv!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb8e4f62c-a946-4705-9128-65a5d82af519_4032x3024.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7Sbv!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb8e4f62c-a946-4705-9128-65a5d82af519_4032x3024.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7Sbv!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb8e4f62c-a946-4705-9128-65a5d82af519_4032x3024.jpeg\" width=\"4032\" height=\"3024\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/b8e4f62c-a946-4705-9128-65a5d82af519_4032x3024.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:3024,&quot;width&quot;:4032,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:2563181,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://chillphysicsenjoyer.substack.com/i/208724777?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F33f90996-a4de-4351-8fb5-20c2e2da9353_4032x3024.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7Sbv!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb8e4f62c-a946-4705-9128-65a5d82af519_4032x3024.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7Sbv!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb8e4f62c-a946-4705-9128-65a5d82af519_4032x3024.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7Sbv!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb8e4f62c-a946-4705-9128-65a5d82af519_4032x3024.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!7Sbv!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb8e4f62c-a946-4705-9128-65a5d82af519_4032x3024.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Here were the question prompts. Often times the discussions did stray away from these prompts though, but that\u2019s fine.</p><h2>Why?</h2><ul><li><p>What is the point of writing science?</p><ul><li><p>What is the job of the scientist?</p></li><li><p>What is good science writing?</p><ul><li><p>Should we care at all about writing good science - whatever that is?</p></li><li><p>If so how frequently do we need to write?</p></li></ul></li><li><p>Is there a point in writing science ourselves given LLMs exist now?</p><ul><li><p>Is there a way to get past the human vs LLM competition and still be marginally useful?</p></li></ul></li><li><p>Is the human act of writing science still worthwhile?</p></li><li><p>Do we expect the purpose of scientific writing today to change?</p><ul><li><p>Will scientific writing soon become purely a pedagogical act?</p></li><li><p>If AI provides all the answers then shouldn't we be optimising for human understanding, like Terence Tao's recent digestions on the Jacobian conjecture counter examples.</p></li></ul></li></ul></li><li><p>How many people need to read a piece of science for it to become common knowledge?</p><ul><li><p>Does it matter who these people are?</p></li><li><p>Does the buck stop at experiment replication?</p></li></ul></li></ul><h2>Credibility</h2><ul><li><p>Should we be optimising for legitimacy or the appearance of credibility in any way? And if so why, and to whom?</p><ul><li><p>Will scientific experts matter any more given LLMs?</p></li></ul></li><li><p>Are there any credibility structures that still remain that get in the way of communicating the science we do?</p></li></ul><h2>Form and Medium</h2><ul><li><p>Is the written word optimal for communicating science?</p><ul><li><p>Is the traditional scientific paper optimal for communicating science?</p></li><li><p>Does the written word have enough information density?</p></li><li><p>If not, why not videos / audio / pictures?</p><ul><li><p>Or why not everything at once?</p></li><li><p>In practical terms how do we host the optimal form of communication on servers?</p></li></ul></li></ul></li><li><p>What are the optimal ways for feedback and replication?</p></li></ul><h2>Polished-ness And Thought Privacy</h2><ul><li><p>How much of our thinking process should we expose to the public?</p></li><li><p>How much can authors change their mind without damaging credibility?</p></li><li><p>How good does something have to be before it is written?</p></li><li><p>Should government funded scientists write more and more often?</p></li><li><p>How do we trade off the time spent writing versus actually doing the thing?</p></li></ul><h2>Clarity And Detail</h2><ul><li><p>Clarity and detail are opposing things - how do we trade them off?</p></li><li><p>What does it mean for writing to be clear?</p><ul><li><p>How do we write clearly?</p></li><li><p>How can we tell if an expression of idea becomes too complex?</p></li><li><p>How much exactness do we need for someone to be able to replicate our experiment to a reasonable level of sameness?</p></li><li><p>What about style?</p></li></ul></li><li><p>Does scientific writing <strong>need</strong> to be clear given AI?</p></li><li><p>Who are we trying to be clear for?</p></li><li><p>How do we trade off clarity for time?</p></li><li><p>Is clarity audience dependent?</p></li></ul><h2>Ethics</h2><ul><li><p>How do we think about writing science that could be used for nefarious purposes?</p><ul><li><p>A question in particular for the bio writers out there!</p></li></ul></li></ul>",
